WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.010 --> 00:00:09.010
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and this is going
to be my combined episode 8 and 9 review.

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:14.200
I’ll do a quick run through of my biggest
takeaways from episode 8 and just do the normal

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:17.289
top 5 and review for episode 9. I feel like
the last couple of weeks have really shown

00:00:17.289 --> 00:00:21.430
why MTV chose to not just renew it for a season
5, but for a full 20 episodes. They’re splitting

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:21.970
it up into two parts just like season 3. I’ll
explain more about what’s happening at the

00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:22.090
end of the video.

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:25.150
So careful for spoilers from the last two
episodes if you’re not current. Starting

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:26.869
with Episode 8 commentary.

00:00:26.869 --> 00:00:31.730
My oh shit panic moment is Derek losing his
powers. We’re a little past halfway in the

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:36.539
season and we still don’t have any new info
on what Kate did to him. I totally hate that

00:00:36.539 --> 00:00:39.839
it’s destroying the Derek we knew but I
love the Derek he’s turning into.

00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:45.249
Think back to Season 1 and 2 Derek, he was
a total dick. Now he’s like the Obi-Wan

00:00:45.249 --> 00:00:49.799
Kenobi big brother to everyone. So much more
sympathetic and if Tyler Hoechlin is probably

00:00:49.799 --> 00:00:53.019
going to make you cry a lot before the finale.

00:00:53.019 --> 00:00:56.889
He is coming back for season 5, so it’s
not like he’s dying for good. Despite what

00:00:56.889 --> 00:01:00.119
the Banshee Benefactor has predicted. But
I feel like he hasn’t hit rock bottom yet,

00:01:00.119 --> 00:01:03.299
things are still going to get worse. But if
he does have to get his ass handed to him

00:01:03.299 --> 00:01:05.590
at least he’s got Braeden.

00:01:05.590 --> 00:01:10.880
Great Sex Scene. Not HBO levels of skin, but
I was still really happy to see them get together.

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:15.610
I also like the way they paired the sex scene
visually with the table full of guns. There’s

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:19.080
all kinds of imagery going on with those two
things that I could spend 6 videos talking

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:19.720
about.

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:23.950
Which leads me to the big reveal. The Benefactor
is a Banshee, only they can confirm death

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:29.430
without seeing a body. Scott’s death sequence
wasn’t quite as trippy as the ones in season

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:34.500
3 but I liked the way they used Liam. I think
Scott’s unconscious mind was just processing

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:35.110
his fears.

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:39.720
He has alpha powers, but I don’t think that
gives him straight up foresight like Lydia

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:46.720
has. It’s probably just his wolf spidey-sense
interacting with all the current worries he

00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:50.520
has for Liam and the others.

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:54.210
Lydia’s Grandmother didn’t end up quite
the way I expected, but I’ll talk more about

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:55.840
that when I get to episode 9.

00:01:55.840 --> 00:02:02.110
Malia is kind of pushed to the side. I think
we’re all feeling she’ll eventually come

00:02:02.110 --> 00:02:05.850
back to the pack. Not right away, but there’s
no way she’s over Stiles. I think he’s

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:09.159
her anchor, so she’ll always come back.
Her scene with Peter wasn’t quite as diabolical

00:02:09.159 --> 00:02:12.670
as I expected either. I was expecting him
to get a little more shakespearean. But I

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:16.319
am really interested in the new mystery of
Malia’s mother. I actually thought Peter

00:02:16.319 --> 00:02:21.480
had an affair with Henry Tate’s wife, but
turns out her biological mother is something

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:28.299
more coyote-like. Which is pretty adorable.
Let me know when you think we’ll meet her

00:02:28.299 --> 00:02:31.879
mother or if you think they’ll hold off
till season 5 to reveal her.

00:02:31.879 --> 00:02:36.159
Overall episode 8 was a solid B plus, great
character development for Derek, nice seeding

00:02:36.159 --> 00:02:40.370
of new plotlines with Malia’s mother and
Lydia’s Grandmother. Kira felt like she

00:02:40.370 --> 00:02:44.900
got pushed to the side a little for these
other stories despite being a pretty critical

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:50.549
part of their plan. I’m waiting for more
Lacrosse so she can kick some butt.

00:02:50.549 --> 00:02:55.040
Moving on to Episode 9, again, one more time,
if you haven’t seen it, careful for spoilers.

00:02:55.040 --> 00:03:01.799
I’ll wait just a sec...okay, here we go.
Top 5 moments. Starting with Number 5 - Parrish

00:03:01.799 --> 00:03:03.010
On Fire

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:06.919
This was probably my favorite moment in general
and the perfect opening to an episode. I just

00:03:06.919 --> 00:03:10.290
made it my number 5 because I wanted to talk
about it first. They don’t even bother to

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:16.889
explain things in great detail. The title
of the episode was Perishable. That other

00:03:16.889 --> 00:03:23.840
deputy is Lou Ferrigno’s son in real life
by the way. The Hulk’s son is a villain.

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:24.709
Totally makes sense.

00:03:24.709 --> 00:03:29.529
Dissecting what he might be: I think he’s
either a twist on something we’ve seen or

00:03:29.529 --> 00:03:34.769
something totally new. But he’s not just
exactly like anyone in the pack. Part of this

00:03:34.769 --> 00:03:40.040
season has been about the wide variety of
supernatural creatures in beacon hills.

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:44.419
We’ve got Werewolves, Lightning Kitsunes,
Banshee’s, Wendigos and now whatever he

00:03:44.419 --> 00:03:49.299
is. Here’s a quick list of mythological
creatures that are resistant to fire:

00:03:49.299 --> 00:03:55.749
Fire Kitsunes, Kira is a lightning kitsune,
but fire is the other kind. There’s Dragons,

00:03:55.749 --> 00:04:02.489
Phoenixes, Jinn, Firebirds, Chimera, Salamanders.
Just to explain that one, in Ancient Greek,

00:04:02.489 --> 00:04:07.120
the word for Salamander means “being that
lives in fire and withstands high temperatures”.

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:13.129
Then there’s Kapre, Fire Giants, Cherufe
and Fire Serpents.

00:04:13.129 --> 00:04:17.840
Of all those things, I think it’s more likely
he’s a fire kitsune or a phoenix. If you

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:21.739
look at the way Kira’s powers work, she
absorbs electrical discharge. I don’t know

00:04:21.739 --> 00:04:25.690
if she can still be burnt by electricity but
I don’t think so. Which makes me think that

00:04:25.690 --> 00:04:30.360
Parrish is a phoenix, because he looked like
he burnt in the fire, then regenerated himself.

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:37.360
I don’t expect them to reveal what his till
the end of the season, but I’m glad he’s

00:04:39.850 --> 00:04:46.850
working inside the pack now. I think it just
means he’s going to be an official member

00:04:48.530 --> 00:04:55.530
of the team in 

00:05:12.650 --> 00:05:14.090
season 5.

00:05:14.090 --> 00:05:15.980
Number 4 - Lydia’s Grandmother Is Explained

00:05:15.980 --> 00:05:20.280
I was totally expecting her to end up being
the benefactor, her background in tech was

00:05:20.280 --> 00:05:24.730
a nice twist and I really appreciate that
they took the time to give her a very detailed

00:05:24.730 --> 00:05:26.840
backstory.

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:31.020
Visually the way they filmed the flashback
with Lydia walking in and out of scenes was

00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:35.910
awesome. Usually they post really cool looking
scenes like that online at some point just

00:05:35.910 --> 00:05:42.910
to show you how they shot them. For anyone
that’s interested in filmmaking.

00:05:44.960 --> 00:05:46.800
Number 3 - Liam Goes Crazy

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:52.060
He’s having this Jack Nicholson Shining
arc where he slowly goes crazier and crazier.

00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:55.620
All work and no play make Liam a dull beta.
They’ll have to resolve that at some point

00:05:55.620 --> 00:05:59.280
because at the party he was trying to drown
himself in alcohol. Despite not being able

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:05.190
to get drunk because of their healing factor.

00:06:05.190 --> 00:06:09.650
Just to be clear, all the printers were printing
the deapool list, to everywhere in beacon

00:06:09.650 --> 00:06:11.500
hills.

00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:18.500
I wonder what made Liam jump to 18 Million
dollars though. It seems like the whole pack

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:21.590
or anyone who’s close to finding out who
the benefactor is would jump in value.

00:06:21.590 --> 00:06:26.530
I think it just means that Liam is more connected
to said Benefactor than we think.

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:30.890
Number 2 - The Bonfire

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:35.270
I loved the way they set this up with Parrish,
making us think that a bunch of people were

00:06:35.270 --> 00:06:40.280
all going to die at the same time. That was
foreshadowing the team going after the pack.

00:06:40.280 --> 00:06:47.210
It seems like the music was just playing some
weird frequency that stupefied them.

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:52.310
This was like the logical breaking point in
the episode, the oh shit moment, even though

00:06:52.310 --> 00:06:55.470
it totally got upstaged by the benefactor
reveal.

00:06:55.470 --> 00:07:00.050
And my number 1 WTF moment of course: Meredith
is the Benefactor

00:07:00.050 --> 00:07:03.970
There was a whole lot going on during the
eichen house portion of the episode the reveal

00:07:03.970 --> 00:07:09.140
was just the biggest part. I loved Brunski’s
tapes. I bet if you bribed him he’d totally

00:07:09.140 --> 00:07:16.140
make you a mixed tape. I can only imagine
what he’d put on it.

00:07:27.010 --> 00:07:31.390
The twist that he was helping Meredith was
great but I am a little worried that the whole

00:07:31.390 --> 00:07:37.830
thing is going to be a simple revenge story.
Meredith getting revenge on everyone for what

00:07:37.830 --> 00:07:41.480
happened to her. That feels like it would
be a letdown after all the time they spent

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:42.760
teasing this out.

00:07:42.760 --> 00:07:48.000
So many interesting things here though. Brunski
seemed like his character exploded with complexity

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:51.080
right before he died. I guess that’s the
tradeoff, Teen Wolf kills you off, but they

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:53.430
let you make you really interesting before
doing so.

00:07:53.430 --> 00:07:57.160
He said he was helping the inmates by killing
them, I wonder if this was because of some

00:07:57.160 --> 00:08:04.160
creepy religious belief. Like the Faceless
Men in a song of ice and fire. They view murder

00:08:06.630 --> 00:08:13.630
as a sacrament to their god.
He was so great as a creepo though, Peter

00:08:14.060 --> 00:08:18.610
is going to have to get extra creepy to fill
the void. Wouldn’t that be funny if Peter

00:08:18.610 --> 00:08:23.639
became the new caretaker of Eichen House.
I’d totally buy that.

00:08:23.639 --> 00:08:27.620
The whole Benefactor operation seems like
it was localized to Eichen House, as in Meredith

00:08:27.620 --> 00:08:31.490
only made people in there help her. Like Lydia’s
grandmother and Brunski.

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:37.580
It makes you wonder who else is helping her.
Probably not Kate and Peter, they seem like

00:08:37.580 --> 00:08:44.580
they have their own agendas.

00:08:56.880 --> 00:09:03.880
But 
let me know why you think Meredith started
the Deadpool List, why does she want to kill

00:09:07.160 --> 00:09:13.470
all supernatural creatures in Beacon Hills?

00:09:13.470 --> 00:09:16.500
Fingers crossed that it goes deeper than simple
revenge.

00:09:16.500 --> 00:09:19.900
Overall I gave this episode an A minus for
making Parrish one of the most interesting

00:09:19.900 --> 00:09:24.100
characters on the show right now and for not
waiting to pay off the Benefactor Reveal.

00:09:24.100 --> 00:09:26.620
There’s always a risk in waiting too long
to reveal the big villain. If you wait till

00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:26.890
the end of the season and you don’t intend
to carry them over to the next season you

00:09:26.890 --> 00:09:27.150
lose a lot of time letting them get their
Loki swerve on. Meredith being the new Loki

00:09:27.150 --> 00:09:27.190
of the series.

00:09:27.190 --> 00:09:28.779
Clearly she’s been faking her disability
this whole time. And now we get 3 more episodes

00:09:28.779 --> 00:09:32.540
with her being this crazy villain on screen.

00:09:32.540 --> 00:09:36.930
I wonder if they learned their lesson last
season with waiting too long to reveal Jennifer

00:09:36.930 --> 00:09:41.220
in 3A and Nugitsune Stiles in 3B. I would
have liked to see a lot more of Stiles as

00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:43.460
a supervillain going crazy all over everyone.

00:09:43.460 --> 00:09:46.880
Let me know what you think. Do you like finding
out who the main villain is in the middle

00:09:46.880 --> 00:09:49.800
of the season or right before the end?

00:09:49.800 --> 00:09:53.290
I think revealing them earlier just lets you
have more fun with them but I can understand

00:09:53.290 --> 00:09:54.990
not wanting to show them right away.

00:09:54.990 --> 00:10:01.990
This season has gotten better and better.
All the characters feel more relatable, the

00:10:04.490 --> 00:10:08.580
plot isn’t so crazy it’s distracting and
the return of Lacrosse has been so much fun.

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:10.540
Especially Kira and Lacrosse.

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:15.470
Right now the wiki is listing the remaining
three episodes airing each week with no breaks.

00:10:15.470 --> 00:10:20.250
Episode 10 is Monstrous, I’m hoping that
means they explain Parrish. Episode 11 is

00:10:20.250 --> 00:10:25.210
“A Promise to the Dead”, hopefully that
will explain Meredith’s backstory and they

00:10:25.210 --> 00:10:29.330
haven’t revealed the title of the finale.
Probably because it’s something spoilery.

00:10:29.330 --> 00:10:33.950
Important stuff happening this week: Doctor
Who is back this saturday, if you’re not

00:10:33.950 --> 00:10:40.950
watching it you should start. It is the most
fun science fiction you will ever watch. And

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:47.290
I’m doing a ton of videos for it like I
did for game of thrones.

00:10:47.290 --> 00:10:51.750
I’m moving next week too but my video schedule
should be normal. I had my last day at work

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:53.820
friday so I have a little more time to actually
make stuff. I will do a room tour video after

00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:55.620
I move into my new place.

00:10:55.620 --> 00:11:01.960
In the meantime click here to start getting
ready for Doctor Who and click here for last

00:11:01.960 --> 00:11:02.300
week’s teen wolf.

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:03.040
Thanks for watching, see you guys tonight.
High Fives!

